{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that observes the dispatch cycle and forwards events to a provider-agnostic "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unlike the gate-style plugins ("},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), analytics is an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"observer"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it watches actions flow by and emits events, but never blocks dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two surfaces:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mapper (passive)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — App declares a "},{"code":"(state, action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure once at registration. The plugin runs it in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (explicit)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Screen views, identify\/alias\/reset, ad-hoc tracks, and opt-out toggling. For the things passive observation can’t cover cleanly."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plus optional "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"auto-identify"}]},{"type":"text","text":": pass an "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keypath and the plugin watches userID transitions across dispatches, firing "},{"code":"service.identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"service.reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For end-to-end wiring, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":". For where this plugin sits in the lifecycle, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","level":2,"text":"Library target"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to your target dependencies in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Provided-implementations","level":2,"text":"Provided implementations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin ships with two in-repo conformers, both provider-agnostic and SDK-free:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MockAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — silent no-op, for previews and tests."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ConsoleAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — logs every call to "},{"code":"os.Logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Use this as the default "},{"code":"service:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" while the analytics vendor decision is still open: analytics wiring can be developed and QA-tested end to end with no SDK and no vendor commitment. Adopting a real provider later is the usual two-line change in "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For production Mixpanel integrations, the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" companion package provides:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — an "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that forwards to the Mixpanel SDK and maps "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to native Mixpanel types."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — a Mixpanel-flavored mock for previews."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full API documentation lives in the package’s own "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For other backends (Amplitude, PostHog, Segment, custom), implement "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directly — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" Step 3, Path B."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Types","level":2,"text":"Types"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsPlugin%3CRootState-RootAction%3E","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsPlugin<RootState, RootAction>`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"final class","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer. Owns a slice of root state typed as "},{"code":"AnalyticsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and an action enum typed as "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public init(","    state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, AnalyticsState>,","    action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (AnalyticsAction) -> RootAction,","    extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> AnalyticsAction?,","    service: any AnalyticsService,","    mapper: AnalyticsMapper<RootState, RootAction> = .none,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity<RootState>? = nil,","    onConsentChange: (@Sendable (Bool) async -> Void)? = nil",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"onConsentChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fires on every "},{"code":".setOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatch with the new opted-out value. Use it to drive a vendor SDK’s own consent API — see "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Consent"}]},{"type":"text","text":" below."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin is a "},{"code":"final class","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (not a struct) because it tracks pending fire-and-forget service calls so that "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can deterministically await them — same reason "},{"code":"PersistencePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"UndoPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are classes."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsState","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsState`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" struct. The slice the plugin owns."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var isOptedOut: Bool","    public var currentScreen: String?","    public internal(set) var lastIdentifiedUserID: String?","","    public init(isOptedOut: Bool = false, currentScreen: String? = nil)","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — App-controlled privacy flag. While "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mapper events are dropped, explicit "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actions become no-ops, and auto-identify is paused."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — The most recent screen recorded via "},{"code":".screenView(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", auto-attached as the "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property on subsequent tracked events."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Set by the plugin (read-only from outside the module). Used to detect identity transitions."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsAction","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsAction`"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum AnalyticsAction: Sendable, Equatable {","    case track(AnalyticsEvent)","    case screenView(String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue])","    case identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue])","    case alias(newID: String, previousID: String?)","    case reset","    case setOptedOut(Bool)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Convenience factories cover the common no-properties cases:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".screenView(\"Profile\")                    \/\/ properties: [:]",".identify(userID: \"u1\")                   \/\/ properties: [:]",".alias(newID: \"user-42\")                  \/\/ previousID: nil"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsEvent","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsEvent`"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsEvent: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var name: String","    public var properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]","","    public init(_ name: String, _ properties: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [:])","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsValue","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsValue`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Closed enum keeping the protocol provider-agnostic and "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each service adapter maps these cases to its native property type."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum AnalyticsValue: Sendable, Equatable {","    case string(String)","    case int(Int)","    case double(Double)","    case bool(Bool)","    case date(Date)","    case array([AnalyticsValue])","    case dict([String: AnalyticsValue])","    case null","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Literal conformances keep call-sites clean:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let props: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [","    \"amount\": 5,           \/\/ .int","    \"tier\": \"pro\",         \/\/ .string","    \"active\": true,        \/\/ .bool","    \"ratio\": 0.5,          \/\/ .double","    \"tags\": [\"a\", \"b\"],    \/\/ .array","]"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsMapper%3CState-Action%3E","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsMapper<State, Action>`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wraps the declarative "},{"code":"(state, action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsMapper<State, Action>: Sendable {","    public typealias Map = @Sendable (State, Action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","    public let map: Map","    public init(_ map: @escaping Map)","    public static var none: AnalyticsMapper { ... }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returning an empty array is the no-op case. "},{"code":".none","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default mapper for plugins that only use explicit "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatches."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsIdentity%3CState%3E","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsIdentity<State>`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarative source-of-truth for the active user’s identity."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsIdentity<State>: Sendable {","    public let userID: @Sendable (State) -> String?","    public let userProperties: @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue]","","    public init(","        userID: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> String?,","        userProperties: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue] = { _ in [:] }","    )","","    public init(","        userID keyPath: KeyPath<State, String?> & Sendable,","        userProperties: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue] = { _ in [:] }","    )","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The KeyPath convenience init is the typical shape: "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.auth.currentUserID)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsService-protocol","level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsService` (protocol)"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsService: Sendable {","    func track(_ event: AnalyticsEvent) async","    func identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]) async","    func alias(newID: String, previousID: String?) async","    func reset() async","    func flush() async","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementations own batching, retry, network failure handling, and offline queueing. The plugin invokes "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fire-and-forget; only "},{"code":"flush","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is awaited."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"MockAnalyticsService","level":3,"text":"`MockAnalyticsService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No-op conformer for previews and development."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct MockAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init()","    \/\/ All methods are no-ops.","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"ConsoleAnalyticsService","level":3,"text":"`ConsoleAnalyticsService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Logs every "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"flush","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"os.Logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with a recursive pretty-printer for "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The recommended default before a vendor is chosen."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ConsoleAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init(subsystem: String = \"Swidux\", category: String = \"Analytics\")","    \/\/ Each call logs one structured line; output visible in","    \/\/ the Xcode console and Console.app, quiet in Release.","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Action-semantics","level":2,"text":"Action semantics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each case below describes the state mutation the plugin performs and the effect (if any) it returns."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"trackAnalyticsEvent","level":3,"text":"`track(AnalyticsEvent)`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.track(event)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" auto-attached as the "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property if the event doesn’t already specify one. Skipped entirely (returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") when opted out. No state mutation."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"screenViewString-properties","level":3,"text":"`screenView(String, properties:)`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the given name "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"regardless of opt-out"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (the screen state still progresses for when the user opts back in). Returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"code":"\"screen_view\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event whose properties include "},{"code":"screen_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plus any extras. Skipped (returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") when opted out."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"identifyuserID-properties","level":3,"text":"`identify(userID:, properties:)`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID = userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Skipped when opted out. Use this when the app needs to force identity before the auto-identify keypath would observe the change."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"aliasnewID-previousID","level":3,"text":"`alias(newID:, previousID:)`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No state mutation. Returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Skipped when opted out. Call once when an anonymous user signs up to link the anonymous distinct ID to the new user ID."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"reset","level":3,"text":"`reset`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Runs even when opted out — "},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is by definition a clean-slate operation."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"setOptedOutBool","level":3,"text":"`setOptedOut(Bool)`"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"setOptedOut(true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Sets "},{"code":"isOptedOut = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", clears "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", returns an effect that invokes "},{"code":"onConsentChange(true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and then calls "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to clear server-side identity."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"setOptedOut(false)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Clears the flag. Returns an effect invoking "},{"code":"onConsentChange(false)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when no hook is configured. Auto-identify on the next dispatch will re-establish identity."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Consent","level":2,"text":"Consent"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opting out is enforced "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"plugin-side"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"screenView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the mapper, and auto-identify all return early while "},{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so nothing reaches the service. Only "},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"flush","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" still pass through."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That gate stops Swidux-dispatched events. It does not touch the vendor SDK’s own consent switch — so an SDK configured to collect automatic events, or one still holding a queue of its own, can keep sending after the user opts out. "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" deliberately stays at five members (consent APIs differ too much between vendors to abstract, and only the app knows which one it is using), so the bridge is the "},{"code":"onConsentChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Semantics: it fires on every "},{"code":".setOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatch with the new value, and on opt-out it runs "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the SDK’s opt-out closes the tap before the reset hands it an identity change that is still eligible to be sent. Events already in flight are not retracted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Treat this as required wiring for any vendor with a consent API, not an optional extra: without it, “opted out” means only that Swidux stopped sending. See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" Step 9 for the wiring."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Mapper-semantics","level":2,"text":"Mapper semantics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mapper runs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in. The plugin:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Skips entirely if the action is an "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (handled by "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already, no double-tracking)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Skips when "},{"code":"state.isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls "},{"code":"mapper.map(state, action)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and tracks each returned event via "},{"code":"service.track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" auto-attached as "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (unless the event already provides its own "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returning an empty array is the no-op case. The mapper closure is allowed to read freely from the post-reducer state — that’s deliberately what gets passed in."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Auto-identify-semantics","level":2,"text":"Auto-identify semantics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When configured with an "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the plugin re-evaluates both the "},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closures each non-analytics dispatch and diffs the pair "},{"code":"(userID, userProperties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against the last value sent to the service:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"nil → \"u1\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (sign-in): updates "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", fires "},{"code":"service.identify(userID:\"u1\", properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\"u1\" → \"u2\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (account switch): updates both, fires "},{"code":"service.identify(userID:\"u2\", properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable userID, "},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" content changed: updates "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", fires "},{"code":"service.identify(userID:, properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the new dictionary."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\"u1\" → nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (sign-out): clears both, fires "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable userID and stable "},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": no-op."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is re-evaluated every non-analytics dispatch; dictionary equality decides whether to re-fire "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This keeps derived people-properties (subscription tier, paywall entitlements, feature flags) in sync with state without any explicit "},{"code":".identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plumbing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When opted out, auto-identify is paused: neither "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" nor "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is updated. Opting back in re-establishes identity correctly on the next dispatch."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Flushing","level":2,"text":"Flushing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" awaits any pending fire-and-forget service calls spawned by "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then calls "},{"code":"service.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Call this on app shutdown to avoid losing in-flight events:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await store.analyticsPlugin.flush() }","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Implementing-an-AnalyticsService","level":2,"text":"Implementing an `AnalyticsService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin is provider-agnostic. Your conformer is responsible for translating "},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into whatever the backend SDK expects."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol has five methods, all "},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and non-throwing. Errors are the service’s responsibility: log them, queue for retry, drop them — whatever fits your backend’s reliability model. The plugin will not see them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typical Mixpanel conformer holds a reference to the "},{"code":"Mixpanel.Instance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and translates "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"MixpanelType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An Amplitude conformer holds an "},{"code":"Amplitude","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance and translates to "},{"code":"[String: Any]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Either way, the plugin stays the same."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note what the protocol does "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" require: no opt-out flag (the plugin handles that), no super-property machinery for "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the plugin handles that), and no event batching policy (your call)."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Macros","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","kind":"article","title":"Add Analytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"role":"collection","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"https://heirloomlogic.github.io/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/swiduxmixpanelanalytics/":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC reference"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","url":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","title":"DocC reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","role":"article","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"Public API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","title":"KeyValueStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"}}}